<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>40% of the oil wells in Kuwait were/are owned by the Bush family oil company; starting to see the connection?</b><hr></blockquote><br>
I'm not so sure this is a fact, I'd like to see your source.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>China has a lot more to lose and a lot less of a motivation. Many of the terrorist groups to which I allude are religious groups that view the US as a kind of Satanic power that is to be fought at all costs. This makes them much more dangerous than an established power like China that has quite a bit at stake. China relies on the US for export and import revenues and goods. The terrorist groups do not.</b><hr></blockquote><br>
Got a news flash for you here bub: China's government <b>is</b> a religous group, worshipping an irrational belief that the completely impractical, namely communism, will work.  They are every bit as fanatical as the Islamic Jihad, and every bit as irrational.  And far more dangerous.  Last I looked, the Jihad didn't have nukes.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>Its not the aircrew that I hold responsible. Its a government that continues military campaigns of international espionage. The crew I hold responsible for not being skeptical enough to say,"Do we really need to be doing this?"</b><hr></blockquote><br>
And I hold you responsible for not knowing that this is not an option for a member of the military.  If you wear the uniform, you either follow the orders, or you get court-martialed.  There is no point where you can say "I don't want to do this", unless you are convinced that the order you have been given is illegal.  Flying a surveillance plane over international waters is in no way illegal, refusing the order would have resulted in court-martial leading to revocation of commission for the officers and court-martial leading to <b>prison sentence</b> for the enlisted.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>You're a pilot and I'm more than willing to take your word for it. I stand corrected.</b><hr></blockquote><br>
No, I'm not a pilot.  Merethena is the pilot, I refer you to her earlier comments for testimony on just how insane it was that China should blame our pilots for this accident.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>Rosevelt and the cabinet members knew about the raid as much as 18 hours in advance. No mention was passed on to the CO at Pearl Harbor. Did we need to get involved in WWII? Yes, I believe so. Did Pearl Harbor need to happen? No, I believe not.</b><hr></blockquote><br>
Recent discoveries place this assertion in doubt.  Did they suspect an attack was coming?  Yes.  They suspected sabotage as well, which is why all of our planes and ships were in nice tight formations on the ground and in the harbor.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>See what I wrote above. Conflict of interest much?</b><hr></blockquote><br>
Show me your source.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>*cough cough*<br>
<br>
/em points to the Japanese internment camps of WWII and the indian reservations.<br>
<br>
Albiet that was Democraps and Repugnicans, I guess simple ethnicity was good enough for them.</b><hr></blockquote><br>
I said political views, and I meant it.  I'm not referring to ethnicity.  While it could be argued that putting people in prison for drug offenses is holding them for a political action, we don't as yet put them there for advocating legalisation.<br>
<br>
<b><blockquote><FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >quote:</font><hr>Again, I reiterate, why are we spying?</b><hr></blockquote><br>
Again, I reiterate, because China has nukes.  Last I checked, we spy on <b>everyone</b> who has nukes, even our closest allies.  If you're so naive' that you think spying is an outmoded form of behavior, well....<br>
